# Conventions Rules (P2) — Coding & Format Standards

## C-1 — Pre-Commit Verification Checklist

Before committing, verify `python -m pytest tests/ -q`, `ruff check src/ tests/`,
`ruff format --check src/ tests/`, no absolute paths in agent-facing files,
and CHANGELOG updates for user-visible changes.

Source: CP-7.

## C-2 — Lean Message Format

TaskDispatch and StatusReport MUST use the lean formats in
`schemas/lean-dispatch.yaml` and `schemas/lean-report.yaml`; verbose prose is
prohibited. Use verbatim `key_facts` and cause→effect notation. Predecessor
`key_facts` and report `delta` MUST be source extractions: never paraphrase
paths, errors, metrics, or commit hashes (CO-1/CO-2).

Source: CO-1; CO-2.

## C-4 — Tiered Line Budget

Tiered ceilings: Default `<500` lines for `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md`;
Large `≤1000` for `references/*.md` (26 files); XL `≤1600` for
`examples/*.md` (3 files).

Verify with:
```bash
wc -l workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md workflow-system/agent/references/*.md workflow-system/agent/examples/*.md
python -m pytest tests/test_integration.py::test_skill_md_under_500_lines tests/test_reference_size_budgets.py -v
```

### Required SKILL.md Frontmatter Keys

Frontmatter MUST include ALL: `id`, `version`, `purpose`, `triggers`, `tier`,
`token_estimate`, `last_updated`, `name`, `description`. `description` MUST
state WHEN/WHY to activate, not WHAT it does. Verify with the C-4 commands.
Source: SF-1; SF-2.

## C-6 — Version Consistency

The version MUST match `src/devolaflow/__init__.py::__version__` in all 7:

1. SKILL.md frontmatter, banner, and `Current version:`
2. `workflow-skill.yaml` identity
3. `pyproject.toml`
4. `scripts/generate_human_docs.py::SOURCE_VERSION`
5. `tests/test_smoke.py`
6. README example (`DevolaFlow vX.Y.Z`)
7. `packages/npm/package.json` (publish workflow tag check)

The README badge is **DERIVED, not pattern-managed (v14.4.0 G-031)**: it is a
dynamic TOML derivation; benchmark-results derives the displayed version from
`version-timeline/versions.json`. Its marked `file://` `SAMPLE_DATA` fallback
MAY lag and is not synced. Use
`scripts/bump_version.py`, then run `python -m pytest tests/test_version.py -v`.

Source: SF-3. Absorbs W-10 (CP-3) — v15.0.0 fold per v15-ADR-004; see v15-ADR-008 §1.

## C-7 — Valid Reference Links

Every `references/xxx.md` cited by SKILL.md MUST exist under
`workflow-system/agent/references/`. The SF-4 set is owned by
`tests/ghost/test_registries.py::_SF4_REFERENCE_SET` and pinned by
`test_skill_reference_links_match_sf4_set`. A new reference MUST add (a) the
file, (b) the SF-4 entry, (c) a SKILL Tier-2 row, and (d) the
`workflow-system/agent/manifest.yaml::references` entry. That manifest is the
install SSOT for `sync_cursor_skill.py::MIRRORED_FILES`, `scripts/install.sh`,
and `devola-init`; parity is tested by `tests/test_install_manifest.py`.
`scripts/scaffold_reference.py` automates (a), (c), and (d). Source: SF-4.

### Lightweight Agent Workspace Artifacts

Files in `.local/.agent/active/<change-id>/` and
`.local/.agent/archive/<date>-<id>/` use these token budgets:

| File | Soft | Hard |
|---|---:|---:|
| goal.md | 200 | 400 |
| checklist.md | 1200 | 2400 |
| stage.md | 400 | 800 |
| preflight.md | 600 | 1200 |
| harness_preflight.md | 800 | 1600 |
| pathfinder_report.md | 800 | 1600 |
| spec.md | 1500 | 3000 |
| STATUS.yaml | 150 | 300 |
| owned_files.txt | 50 | 100 |
| Handoff envelope | 600 | 1200 |
| evidence/ | No token limit | ≤ 10 KB/file; ≤ 50 KB/directory |
| entrance.md | 400/800 |

Soft budget overages warn; Hard ceiling breaches fail commit.

`.local/human/` uses token-only budgets (line/word counts are guidance):

| `input/constitution.md` | 800/1500 |
| `input/requirements.md`, `input/requirements/<domain>.md` | 1200/2500 |
| `input/amendments/<date>-<slug>.md` | 400/800 |
| `output/DIGEST.md` | 600/1000 |
| `output/convergence/<version>-convergence.md` | 700/1000 |

Verify with:
```bash
python -m devolaflow.agent_workspace.lint <change-id>   # agent-workspace artifacts
python -c "from devolaflow.agent_workspace import lint_human; print(lint_human())"  # .local/human/ surface
```
Soft over → warn; hard over → fail commit. Source: v15-ADR-008 §C-9;
human details: `references/human-surface.md` §4c.
